a world of old traditions and  constant innovation this is what makes  europe a global leader in so many fields  from automotive to  agri-food or for example from pharma to  fashion  all across the world made in europe  means top quality today  i would like to talk about what we are  doing  to accelerate the recovery and make  europe even more competitive  the pandemic has led to an unprecedented  risk disruption of our single market  this should never happen again  this is why we are working on a single  market emergency instrument  another lesson we have learned is our  dependency on certain raw materials  sourced from only a handful of producers  green and digital technologies currently  depend on a number of scarce  raw materials we must diversify our  supply chains  this is the goal of our action plan on  critical raw materials  this is why we have proposed to create  a european raw materials alliance  and as we speak we are working to update  our industry strategy  our strategy is still designed to ensure  that industry can lead  the twin green and digital transition  but what has changed is both  the speed and the scale of this  transformation  and we need to make sure that our  industry  does not only keep pace with that change  but it should also drive it this  requires significant  public and private investment  with next generation eu we have a  historic opportunity  to provide the public funding  but we also know that public investment  cannot work miracles on its own we have  put forward  a taxonomy for green investment  and a green bond standard and in the  coming months  we will present more detailed rules to  help  you finance the transition  towards carbon neutrality so that  investors  can take fully informed decisions  in these months as we have fought the  virus  we have explored new ways of working  with european industries  building new and agile alliances  where the public sector joins forces  with industry  i want europe to invest in this approach  building new alliances and partnerships  with the private sector  for example our battery alliance  makes a very good story this is  how europe should always work  we shouldn't just work for our industry  but with our industry
 

